{"id":138403493450184,"type":"artist","name":"Cerberus Shoal","artist":null,"year":1994,"weight":13,"info":{"country":"US","begin":"1994","end":"2005","kind":"Group","similar":["Tarentel","Gastr Del Sol","A Minor Forest","Disco Inferno","Cul de Sac","Labradford","Do Make Say Think","Long Fin Killie","Bark Psychosis","The For Carnation"],"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/d2f2a25f6b7ec96452f7a7f086b8aba2/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg","bio":"(Parts of Cerberus Shoal are now Big Blood , Fire on Fire and dilly dilly.)\n\nCerberus Shoal formed in the fall of 1994. Caleb Mulkerin had relocated from his native South Portland, Maine to Boston in order to join Chriss Sutherland and Thomas Rogers who were both attending universities in the area. All three were fresh from the American high school system and aspiring to begin a new way of life as well as a musical group. At that time, the fourth member, guitarist Josh Ogden, traveled weekly from Falmouth, Maine to Boston for rehearsals.","tags":["post-rock","experimental","Avant-Garde","psychedelic","emo"]},"works":[{"id":264945947201542,"type":"album","name":"And Farewell To Hightide","artist":"Cerberus Shoal","year":1997,"weight":6,"yt":"DAtnWeW2fXA","src":"books","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":46854232918187,"type":"album","name":"Element Of Structure/ Permanence","artist":"Cerberus Shoal","year":1997,"weight":10,"yt":"x4btI3wdgNY","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":13018320481353,"name":"Scaruffi 1990s","rank":517,"scaruffi":7.0}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":233241959841485,"type":"album","name":"Homb","artist":"Cerberus Shoal","year":1999,"weight":15,"yt":"uZ0bUGOudDQ","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Sc